        -:  292:     * @param aProperties is an associative array that can be used to tell the library delete
        -:  293:     *                    function anything special, because it can take any number of additional
        -:  294:     *                    named tuning arguments that the plugin is known to support.  The caller
        -:  295:     *                    continues to own this object (plugin may not delete it), and plugins
        -:  296:     *                    should expect it to be optionally NULL.
        -:  297:     *
        -:  298:     * @throw IO_ERROR if there is a problem finding the footprint or the library, or deleting it.
        -:  299:     */
        -:  300:    virtual void FootprintDelete( const wxString& aLibraryPath, const wxString& aFootprintName,
        -:  301:                                  const std::map<std::string, UTF8>* aProperties = nullptr );
        -:  302:
        -:  303:    /**
        -:  304:     * Clear any cached footprint data for the given library path.
        -:  305:     *
        -:  306:     * This is used to free memory after footprints have been loaded into another cache.
        -:  307:     * The default implementation does nothing; plugins with caches should override.
